    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "Done. The full test suite is green.\n\n## What I changed\n\nIn `addOwner` (`OwnerRestControllerV1.java:135`), I added a guard right after the null-default is applied and before the business-day rollover:\n\n```java\nif (owner.getRegistrationDate() == null) {\n    owner.setRegistrationDate(LocalDate.now());\n}\n// A supplied registration date may not be later than the server's current date.\nif (owner.getRegistrationDate().isAfter(LocalDate.now())) {\n    return new ResponseEntity<>(HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST);\n}\nowner.setRegistrationDate(toBusinessDay(owner.getRegistrationDate()));\n```\n\nPlacement rationale:\n- It runs **after** the null-default so an omitted `registrationDate` (which becomes `LocalDate.now()`) is never rejected.\n- It runs **before** `toBusinessDay(...)`, so the check applies to the date the client actually supplied \u2014 the weekend-to-Monday rollover can't turn a valid same-day registration into a spurious 400.\n\n`BUILD SUCCESS` \u2014 the new `AcceptanceTest.errorRejectsFutureDate` (posting `registrationDate: \"2999-01-01\"` and expecting 400) passes, and the full suite reports `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`.",
